+arrow-controlled gravity for 40 seconds and requires a complete turn. It keeps
+the authored masses, damping, friction, rack, and springs, with no motor,
+prescribed motion, or initial spin. Settling and fixed-period steering replays
+also check slider travel, orientation, lateral drift, gear contacts, and joint
+impulses. An independent CPU mesh check samples rack and gear surfaces every
+four frames with the gallery's four substeps, limiting overlap to 2 mm;
+reported contact counts or contact depths alone cannot prove this. Full turns
+require about pi metres of rack travel, so the old one-metre travel assertion
+has been replaced by a check that the rack stays within the follower gear's
+axial reach throughout the replay.
 Export every source through the same shared exporter; no
 scene-specific export path exists.
 
diff --git a/docs/CONTACT_SOLVER.md b/docs/CONTACT_SOLVER.md
index 5f9df4e..8cd1e37 100644
--- a/docs/CONTACT_SOLVER.md
+++ b/docs/CONTACT_SOLVER.md
@@ -110,6 +110,20 @@ a joint target/frame must not invalidate every unrelated contact in the world.
 Joint row history is reset when its authored definition changes or its slot is
 reused.
 
+For intersecting concave triangles that were separated before the substep,
+contact recovery brackets the crossing and reconstructs the separating
+features near impact. Their barycentric witnesses are transported to the
+predicted triangles to measure penetration. The nearest edge at the start of
+the step is not necessarily the contacting feature: retaining its direction
+after a tooth reaches a flank can create a false braking impulse.
+
+The gallery's `--over-top` rigid-constraint test restores public body states
+from an M capture and replays the recorded Right input without changing the
+authored materials or joints. It checks every substep for abrupt momentum
+loss, verifies that the paddle clears the top, and retains the independent
+mesh-penetration checks. Frame-end impulses alone cannot detect a brief spike
+that occurred earlier in that frame.
+
 ## Iterations and diagnostics
 
 The default is ten primal/dual iterations per phase, raised by active joint
